# ARK Equine — Project Rules
# Next.js 14 + TypeScript + Tailwind + WooCommerce Headless
# Backend: WordPress + WooCommerce at https://arkequine.getkgkrunch.com (this is the ONLY backend — no local WP for this project)

# ═════════════════════════════════════════════
# SECTION 0: HARD RULES — read first, no exceptions
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════

## 0.1 NEVER place a real order / complete a real payment

  The user places every real order / test payment themselves, by hand. Never
  complete one on the live WooCommerce checkout (or any hosted payment page it
  redirects to, e.g. Stripe).

  NOT ALLOWED:
  - Clicking "Place Order" / "Pay" on checkout
  - Submitting card numbers (even Stripe test cards) anywhere on checkout
  - Any step whose next click would create a real order or charge

  ALLOWED (needed to build and debug):
  - Reading product, cart, and checkout pages to verify data (price, stock, totals)
  - Calling WooCommerce Store API / REST API read endpoints
  - Adding items to a cart to inspect the response, as long as checkout is never submitted

  If a check cannot be done without ordering, stop and hand it to the user with
  the exact steps instead of doing it.

## 0.2 Claude NEVER touches git — no commit, no push, no branch, nothing

  The user does ALL git operations manually: staging, committing, branching,
  pushing. Claude must never run `git add`, `git commit`, `git push`, or any
  other git command that changes repo state, even if asked to "save progress."
  If git history needs to change, tell the user what to run — do not run it.

## 0.3 Internal / instruction files NEVER go to git

  The client does not need our working docs. Anything created that is an
  instruction, guide, report, context note, or backend hand-off (PDF, DOC/DOCX,
  MD, HTML export, ZIP, plugin zips, etc.) is for us only.

  RULE: the moment such a file is created, add it to .gitignore in the SAME step
  (exact filename, under "Internal working docs"). Since Claude never commits
  (see 0.2), this just means: never leave it in a place the user's own `git add`
  could accidentally pick up — gitignore it immediately.

  Examples: *-CONTEXT.md, *-BACKEND.md, *-REPORT.*, testing-instructions.pdf,
  roadmap exports, local backup zips, this `clauderules` file itself.
  Real source code (src/, public/) is the only thing meant to be committed.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# SECTION G: DESIGN SYSTEM — PIXEL PERFECT (extract live from the real site)
# Rule: match the live site exactly. No guessing, no approximation.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────

## G0. There are no pre-measured tokens yet — go get them

  Unlike a project where colors/fonts/spacing are already extracted, ark-equine's
  values below are NOT yet measured. Before building any component:

  1. Open the real pages in a browser (localhost.arkequine0211.com or
     https://ark-equine.com) with devtools and read the actual computed styles —
     colors, fonts, spacing, radius, button styles — element by element.
  2. Cross-check against the site's own source so values aren't invented:
     - `wp-content/themes/enfold-child/assets/css/kg_custom.css` — site-wide overrides
     - `wp-content/themes/enfold-child/assets/js/kg-custom.js`
     - `wp-content/themes/enfold-child/templates/template-home-landing.php` — has
       inline CSS design tokens for the "ARK Equine" landing hero (fonts: Millar,
       Lato; teal/graphite palette) — a real starting point, verify against live render
     - `wp-content/themes/enfold-child/template-arioneo*.php` + `arioneo/` folder —
       separate branded landing page, own fonts/colors
     - Enfold parent theme options (Theme Options in wp-admin) for the base palette
  3. Once measured, write the exact values into `src/app/globals.css` as :root CSS
     variables (same pattern as below) and extend Tailwind config to reference them.
  4. NEVER hardcode a hex code directly in a component — always use the token name.
  5. Fill in G1–G12 below with real measured numbers as pages are built. Do not
     guess a value "close enough" — re-measure.

## G1. Color Tokens — fill in after measuring (template below)

